  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation per RBC-TOC-02 for 5 patients. Each has a signed progress note; patients with mid-work changes also have a correction addendum.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum doc-00009.\n- Potassium chloride stopped (mr-00076).\n- Pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution: kept home omeprazole and did not order pantoprazole.\n- Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin continued unchanged.\n- Lisinopril was first kept on hold because K was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat BMP on 10/23 (doc-00901) showed K 4.7 and SCr 1.21, so I resumed lisinopril (mr-00072).\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily (doc-00902) was ignored because it isn't signed.\n- **Needs action:** follow-up task task-t0003 for the old K 5.4 is out of date, but the system wouldn't let me cancel it. Please close it.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol was raised to 12.5 mg twice daily per the summary. A signed addendum then arrived (doc-00904) reversing it for bradycardia and lightheadedness, so it is back at 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016).\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 continued.\n- **Flagged to you by message:**\n  - Atorvastatin 80 mg: last filled 03/04, covering only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. I made no change (comm-t0006).\n  - Glipizide 5 mg: filled at an outside pharmacy, prescribed by Dr. Desai. There is no clinic order and the discharge papers don't mention it. I did not order it (comm-t0007).\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril was resumed on the 10/22 labs (SCr 1.08, K 4.6). A new potassium of 5.5 on 10/23 (obs-09002) then arrived, so it is back on hold (mr-00373).\n- Task task-t0018 is due 10/27 for a repeat potassium.\n- Both insulins and rosuvastatin continued.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): SCr 1.12 and K 4.4 on 10/21.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n- The discharge plan's potassium check at 3 days hasn't come back yet.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067)\n- Metformin ER stays on hold. Its only creatinine (1.21) was drawn in the hospital before discharge, so it doesn't meet the discharge condition.\n- Task task-t0013 is due 10/24 to review the post-discharge BMP.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n\nFour items arrived during the work. I reviewed them, acted on each, and closed them in the inbox (inbox-a0001 to a0004). I didn't touch any other inbox items.",
